<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-ga-hodge-dual" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Hodge Dual</title>
    <idx><term>Hodge Dual</term></idx>

    <identity xml:id="ga-hodge-dual-3D">
        <title>The Cross Product as a Dual Wedge Product</title>
        <p>
            In Clifford algebra <m>\mathcal{Cl}(0,3)</m> (Euclidean 3-D space), the standard vector cross product $\vec{a}\times\vec{b}$ is equivalent to the dual of the geometric wedge product $\vec{a}\wedge\vec{b}$ as follows:

                <md>
                    \vec{a}\times\vec{b} = (\vec{a}\wedge\vec{b})\mathcal{I}^{-1}
                </md>
            where <m>\mathcal{I}=\mathbf{e}_1\mathbf{e}_2\mathbf{e}_3</m> is the unit pseudoscalar in <m>\mathcal{Cl}(0,3)</m>.
        </p>
    </identity>
    <remark>
        <md>
          \mathcal{I}^{-1}=-\mathcal{I}
        </md>
    </remark>



</section>
